  "body": "This is an update `TopologyDescription.Sink` and `TopologyDescription.Source`.\r\n\r\nThe original intent for `TopologyDescription` was to provide users with an interface to perform runtime checking of Topologies. However, `TopologyDescription` has relied too heavily on returning strings as representations of various inner components of Topologies such as topics, topic pattern, etc. This PR instead changes the return types to that of the underlying object and relies on the `toString()` method of these objects to maintain their human readable representations.\r\n\r\nMore details are outlined in this PR's corresponding [KIP](https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-321%3A+Update+TopologyDescription+to+better+represent+Source+and+Sink+Nodes).\r\n\r\n### Committer Checklist (excluded from commit message)\r\n- [ ] Verify design and implementation \r\n- [ ] Verify test coverage and CI build status\r\n- [ ] Verify documentation (including upgrade notes)\r\n",
